  "id": "Compound::DB08877 - Disease::DOID:2531",
  "verbalization": "Ruxolitinib, a protein kinase inhibitor, is linked to Hematologic Cancer through multiple pathways that converge on its shared classification with Nilotinib and Imatinib. The evidence suggests that Ruxolitinib, as a member of the Protein Kinase Inhibitors class, indirectly influences Hematologic Cancer by acting through antineoplastic enzyme inhibitors, which are common in the broader class of antineoplastic compounds. This connection is further supported by the fact that Ruxolitinib causes Prostate Cancer, which is treated by Imatinib, and that Imatinib itself is associated with Hematologic Cancer. The shared ancestry of Ruxolitinib and Imatinib with Organonitrogen Heterocyclic Compounds and Antineoplastic Enzyme Inhibitors underscores a potential mechanism by which Ruxolitinib may contribute to the development of Hematologic Cancer. The evidence highlights a recurring pathway where Ruxolitinib, through its inhibitory effects on specific enzymes, may modulate cellular processes that are implicated in the progression of Hematologic Cancer.",
